1
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,817
I thought you didn't like
taking the lord's name in vain?

2
00:00:06,841 --> 00:00:08,217
Oh, shut up.

3
00:00:11,053 --> 00:00:12,138
It's been a while, huh?

4
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:13,139
Don't blame me.

5
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:14,891
You're the one
who had a heart attack.

6
00:00:15,141 --> 00:00:18,311
Mm, the doctor did say
I needed to get more exercise.

7
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:20,396
I think he meant
walks around the block.

8
00:00:20,605 --> 00:00:21,981
No, he winked at me,

9
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:24,442
and did this little rotation
with his hips, like...

10
00:00:27,737 --> 00:00:28,488
Mm.

11
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:29,696
Hmm.

12
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:31,866
Hey, we got any plans
this weekend?

13
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:35,828
I thought maybe we could get
started on the vegetable garden,

14
00:00:36,037 --> 00:00:37,872
and then, of course,
church on Sunday.

15
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,665
Yeah, that does sound fun,

16
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:42,043
but what if, instead,
I was to go up to bethy creek

17
00:00:42,251 --> 00:00:43,836
with Georgie
and do some fishing?

18
00:00:44,045 --> 00:00:46,297
How long you been waiting
to spring that on me?

19
00:00:46,506 --> 00:00:48,549
Well, not till I was done
rotating my hips.

20
00:00:48,758 --> 00:00:50,218
You're awful.

21
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:53,054
So what do you say?

22
00:00:56,307 --> 00:00:57,308
What about Sheldon?

23
00:00:58,309 --> 00:00:59,309
What about him?

24
00:00:59,435 --> 00:01:00,435
George.

25
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,063
You can't always leave him out.

26
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:03,648
I'm not leaving him out.

27
00:01:03,856 --> 00:01:05,316
You know how
he is about fishing.

28
00:01:06,108 --> 00:01:07,276
Get it away, get it away!

29
00:01:07,485 --> 00:01:08,885
Calm down,
it's an itty-bitty thing.

30
00:01:09,028 --> 00:01:11,030
No, I'm an itty-bitty thing!

31
00:01:11,531 --> 00:01:13,366
Who says you have to
take him fishing?

32
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:14,934
Find something else
to do with him.

33
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:16,035
Something he'd like.

34
00:01:16,244 --> 00:01:17,554
What are we gonna do?
Spend the weekend

35
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:18,871
sitting around, thinking?

36
00:01:19,163 --> 00:01:19,956
George.

37
00:01:20,164 --> 00:01:21,582
You have to make an effort.

38
00:01:21,791 --> 00:01:23,560
Young boys who don't spend
time with their daddies

39
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:25,336
grow up to be oddballs.

40
00:01:25,545 --> 00:01:28,631
Honey, I hate to tell you, but
that ball is already pretty odd.

41
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:31,884
Please.

42
00:01:35,179 --> 00:01:36,264
Okay, fine.

43
00:01:38,266 --> 00:01:39,946
I'll talk to him.
We'll think of something.

44
00:01:40,017 --> 00:01:40,685
Good.

45
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:42,603
Thank you.

46
00:01:45,773 --> 00:01:46,773
What?

47
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:49,777
I was just remembering
when I took him camping.

48
00:01:49,986 --> 00:01:51,112
Sheldon: Moth! Moth!

49
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:52,923
George sr.:
Sheldon, it's just a butterfly.

50
00:01:52,947 --> 00:01:54,073
How is that any better?

51
00:01:54,282 --> 00:01:56,075
Butterfly, butterfly!

52
00:01:58,035 --> 00:02:00,746
J'j' nobody else
is stronger than I am j'j'

53
00:02:00,955 --> 00:02:03,583
j'j' yesterday I moved a mountain j'j'

54
00:02:03,791 --> 00:02:06,210
n I bet I could be your hero I!”

55
00:02:06,419 --> 00:02:09,130
N I am a mighty little man n“

56
00:02:09,338 --> 00:02:12,466
n I am a mighty little man. I!”

57
00:02:21,726 --> 00:02:22,852
Hey, pal

58
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,187
playing with your rockets?

59
00:02:25,438 --> 00:02:28,149
I'm trying to calculate
ballistic coefficients.

60
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,776
Well, that's fun, too.

61
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:32,796
Listen, I don't have
to work this weekend;

62
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,980
I was wondering if you wanted
to do something together.

63
00:02:35,281 --> 00:02:36,281
Like what?

64
00:02:36,741 --> 00:02:37,950
Whatever you want.

65
00:02:38,534 --> 00:02:40,734
Well, the filter on my air
purifier needs to be changed.

66
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:42,121
How about a trip to sears?

67
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,583
Yeah, I was thinking
along the lines of something

68
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:45,665
a little more active.

69
00:02:46,125 --> 00:02:47,125
Like last year,

70
00:02:47,168 --> 00:02:48,168
we went fishing...

71
00:02:48,252 --> 00:02:49,252
Mom! Dad's trying

72
00:02:49,337 --> 00:02:50,463
to make me go fishing!

73
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:52,298
No, no, it's okay.

74
00:02:53,132 --> 00:02:54,425
We're not going fishing.

75
00:02:55,885 --> 00:02:56,927
All right, good.

76
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:58,136
But seriously,

77
00:02:58,471 --> 00:02:59,489
was fishing really that bad?

78
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:01,265
Mom! Dad's trying to convince me

79
00:03:01,474 --> 00:03:02,975
that fishing wasn't that bad!

80
00:03:03,184 --> 00:03:04,310
Shh. Come on!

81
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:05,958
Forget I said anything
about fishing.

82
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:08,105
Just think about it,

83
00:03:08,314 --> 00:03:09,690
and we'll do whatever you want.

84
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:11,524
Thank you.

85
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:17,073
There is the launching of
the space shuttle this weekend.

86
00:03:17,365 --> 00:03:18,574
Space shuttle?

87
00:03:19,075 --> 00:03:20,435
Don't they do those
out of Florida?

88
00:03:20,534 --> 00:03:22,286
Yes. Cape canaveral.

89
00:03:23,871 --> 00:03:26,999
Sheldon, that's-that's like
a12, 15 hour drive.

90
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:30,336
I understand. Never mind.

91
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:33,464
You know what? Let's do it.

92
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:35,132
It'll be fun.

93
00:03:35,341 --> 00:03:37,468
The three Cooper boys
on a little adventure.

94
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:38,885
Sound good?

95
00:03:39,804 --> 00:03:40,888
Sounds good.

96
00:03:43,516 --> 00:03:45,810
Adult Sheldon:
My plan was coming together.

97
00:03:46,018 --> 00:03:47,853
I just needed to get
on the shuttle

98
00:03:48,062 --> 00:03:51,524
so I could finally escape
this ridiculous planet.

99
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:55,069
Spoiler alert, I'm still here.

100
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:56,564
So, Sheldon, me, and Georgie

101
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,577
are gonna take
a little road trip this weekend,

102
00:03:58,614 --> 00:03:59,699
see the shuttle launch.

103
00:04:00,032 --> 00:04:01,534
Looks like I don't
get a vote in this.

104
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,244
Oh, good, you're catching on.

105
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:05,663
I wonder if we'll get
to meet an astronaut.

106
00:04:05,871 --> 00:04:07,248
I remember
when I was a teenager,

107
00:04:07,456 --> 00:04:10,292
I had the biggest crush
on John Glenn.

108
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:12,503
I would've given it up
for him no problem.

109
00:04:12,795 --> 00:04:14,505
- Mom.
- Given what up?

110
00:04:14,755 --> 00:04:16,132
Her allowance. Just eat.

111
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:17,842
So how long
are you gonna be gone?

112
00:04:18,092 --> 00:04:19,653
Oh, we'll leave first thing
Saturday morning,

113
00:04:19,677 --> 00:04:20,696
stay the night in a motel,

114
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:22,972
and see the launch
bright and early on Sunday.

115
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:24,500
I can't believe
we're going to see

116
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:26,600
an actual working spacecraft.

117
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,352
Look how happy he is.

118
00:04:28,561 --> 00:04:29,561
Good job.

119
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:30,771
How come I don't get to go?

120
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,148
'Cause you, me, and meemaw

121
00:04:32,356 --> 00:04:33,649
are gonna have our own fun.

122
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,693
Could we shoot guns
at the gun range?

123
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:37,903
Mm, you're too young
to go to the gun range.

124
00:04:38,112 --> 00:04:39,321
Meemaw took me.

125
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:41,240
We pinky swore.
What are you doing?

126
00:04:41,741 --> 00:04:42,741
Oh, yeah.

127
00:04:42,825 --> 00:04:43,576
Don't listen to me.

128
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:45,619
I don't know what I'm saying.

129
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:52,168
I know you like
to just keep driving,

130
00:04:52,418 --> 00:04:54,271
and get where you're going,
but you can't ignore

131
00:04:54,295 --> 00:04:56,172
- his bathroom schedule.
- I know.

132
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:58,299
He goes number one
first thing in the morning,

133
00:04:58,507 --> 00:05:01,719
then again in the afternoon,
once more in the late afternoon,

134
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:04,346
say 4:00, 4:30,
depending on his juice intake,

135
00:05:04,555 --> 00:05:06,307
and then, a quick piddle
before bedtime.

136
00:05:06,515 --> 00:05:08,726
- "Piddle." got it.
- Now,

137
00:05:08,934 --> 00:05:10,120
number two's a little trickier.

138
00:05:10,144 --> 00:05:11,144
Mary? Relax.

139
00:05:11,187 --> 00:05:12,313
I can take care of my son.

140
00:05:13,314 --> 00:05:13,939
I know.

141
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:14,815
Good.

142
00:05:15,024 --> 00:05:15,816
I'm just saying,

143
00:05:16,025 --> 00:05:17,401
if he's upset or nervous,

144
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:18,736
he can get all clogged up.

145
00:05:18,944 --> 00:05:20,196
I won't let that happen.

146
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:21,696
Thank you.

147
00:05:22,281 --> 00:05:23,401
Okay, let's talk about food.

148
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:24,532
No need to.

149
00:05:25,451 --> 00:05:28,245
He likes his meat cooked
to at least 165 degrees,

150
00:05:28,454 --> 00:05:30,080
except for chicken,
which is 180.

151
00:05:30,289 --> 00:05:32,489
The different foods can't touch
each other on the plate.

152
00:05:32,625 --> 00:05:34,627
Ketchup and mustard
must come out of a packet.

153
00:05:34,877 --> 00:05:35,877
No bottles.

154
00:05:38,214 --> 00:05:39,840
What about his issues
with spaghetti?

155
00:05:41,217 --> 00:05:41,967
That's a trick question.

156
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:43,176
He likes spaghetti.

157
00:05:44,595 --> 00:05:46,096
All right, I guess you got this.

158
00:05:58,734 --> 00:05:59,485
Georgie.

159
00:05:59,693 --> 00:06:00,820
Up and at 'em.

160
00:06:04,406 --> 00:06:05,574
Missy, where's your brother?

161
00:06:05,825 --> 00:06:07,493
Who cares?

162
00:06:15,918 --> 00:06:16,919
Sheldon, you in there?

163
00:06:17,127 --> 00:06:17,753
George Jr.: Dad!

164
00:06:17,962 --> 00:06:18,963
Sorry, Georgie.

165
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:21,465
What's going on?

166
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,384
I can't find Sheldon.

167
00:06:23,968 --> 00:06:25,408
What do you mean,
you can't find him?

168
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:27,346
I mean I don't know where he is.

169
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,640
Well, he's got to be somewhere.

170
00:06:30,099 --> 00:06:32,059
Maybe he got that time machine
to work.

171
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:35,479
Where the hell...

172
00:06:35,688 --> 00:06:37,064
George.

173
00:06:38,774 --> 00:06:40,609
Mary: I think he's ready to go.

174
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:46,657
Mary: Wait, Georgie.

175
00:06:46,866 --> 00:06:48,659
- Where's your bag?
- Don't need one.

176
00:06:48,868 --> 00:06:50,028
Got my toothbrush right here.

177
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,287
What about clothes?

178
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,705
A change of underwear?

179
00:06:53,581 --> 00:06:54,206
Got it.

180
00:06:54,415 --> 00:06:56,500
Georgie, you're gonna
be gone for two days.

181
00:06:56,792 --> 00:06:57,918
I'll turn them inside out.

182
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:00,504
- Shotgun!
- No, no.

183
00:07:00,713 --> 00:07:02,393
Let your brother sit
up front for a change.

184
00:07:02,548 --> 00:07:04,028
I actually prefer
sitting in the back.

185
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:04,925
It's safer.

186
00:07:05,134 --> 00:07:07,386
Oh, come on, sit up front
with your daddy.

187
00:07:07,595 --> 00:07:09,355
He doesn't get to spend
enough time with you.

188
00:07:09,471 --> 00:07:10,848
I called shotgun.

189
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,390
George.

190
00:07:13,434 --> 00:07:14,560
We'll flip a coin.

191
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,562
All right? Georgie, call it.

192
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:17,897
Heads.

193
00:07:19,648 --> 00:07:20,316
Tails.

194
00:07:20,524 --> 00:07:21,684
- Dang it.
- Sheldon, you won.

195
00:07:21,859 --> 00:07:23,027
You get to ride up front.

196
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:24,486
Can't we do two out of three?

197
00:07:24,695 --> 00:07:26,739
You won. Get in the car.

198
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:28,824
What's the point
in calling shotgun?

199
00:07:29,575 --> 00:07:30,618
You're a good dad.

200
00:07:30,826 --> 00:07:33,107
If I don't kill one of them
before Sunday, I'm a good dad.

201
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:35,456
Have fun.

202
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:38,417
Love you guys.

203
00:07:38,626 --> 00:07:40,461
Bye! Drive safe!

204
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:51,263
Oh, this was a good idea,
this was a good idea,

205
00:07:51,472 --> 00:07:52,973
this was a good idea.

206
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:57,853
This was a good idea.

207
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:01,398
Isn't this exciting?

208
00:08:01,607 --> 00:08:04,610
It's just us girls,
no boys in the house.

209
00:08:04,818 --> 00:08:06,098
The place already smells better.

210
00:08:07,196 --> 00:08:08,238
So what are we gonna do?

211
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:09,448
How would you like

212
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:10,866
to go to the beauty salon

213
00:08:11,075 --> 00:08:12,534
and get all done up?

214
00:08:12,785 --> 00:08:14,495
Can I have orange hair
like cyndi lauper?

215
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:16,622
I don't think so.

216
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,832
Meemaw has friends
with blue hair.

217
00:08:19,291 --> 00:08:20,291
She's right.

218
00:08:21,043 --> 00:08:22,086
I haven't gone there yet,

219
00:08:22,294 --> 00:08:24,755
but after a certain age,
it's mandatory.

220
00:08:25,965 --> 00:08:27,508
Your hair's not changing color.

221
00:08:27,716 --> 00:08:29,301
- Aw.
- Sorry, kiddo.

222
00:08:29,885 --> 00:08:31,929
Your mom is no fun.

223
00:08:32,304 --> 00:08:33,847
Excuse me, I'm fun.

224
00:08:34,056 --> 00:08:35,057
So I can color my hair?

225
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:36,308
Not a chance.

226
00:08:36,517 --> 00:08:37,851
But I'm very much fun.

227
00:08:38,936 --> 00:08:40,604
Whatever you need to believe.

228
00:08:40,813 --> 00:08:41,897
Mein fiihrer.

229
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:54,493
Dad?

230
00:08:54,702 --> 00:08:55,702
Yeah?

231
00:08:55,911 --> 00:08:57,997
Would you like
to have a conversation?

232
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:00,332
Yeah. Sure. Absolutely.

233
00:09:00,541 --> 00:09:02,835
All right, what would you
like to talk about?

234
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:06,171
Um, well, let's see.

235
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:09,008
Uh... have you given much
thought to what you want to be

236
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:10,216
when you grow up?

237
00:09:11,093 --> 00:09:12,177
I have.

238
00:09:12,553 --> 00:09:13,553
Great.

239
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:18,726
And what would that be?

240
00:09:20,102 --> 00:09:21,895
Oh. Most likely a scientist.

241
00:09:22,104 --> 00:09:25,524
Unless I stay in Texas,
then I'm thinking cattle baron.

242
00:09:25,733 --> 00:09:26,817
Cattle baron?

243
00:09:27,026 --> 00:09:29,111
Assuming I don't have
to touch the cows.

244
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:31,155
Goes without saying.

245
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,907
Did you always want
to be a football coach?

246
00:09:34,366 --> 00:09:35,659
Well, I always wanted to play.

247
00:09:35,868 --> 00:09:37,119
At least till I got hurt.

248
00:09:37,786 --> 00:09:38,786
Mm.

249
00:09:39,163 --> 00:09:40,414
Were you a good player?

250
00:09:40,622 --> 00:09:42,750
Eh, not really.

251
00:09:42,958 --> 00:09:44,626
I was just bigger
than the other kids.

252
00:09:45,294 --> 00:09:46,962
So you compensated
for mediocrity

253
00:09:47,171 --> 00:09:48,589
by being large.

254
00:09:50,257 --> 00:09:51,258
I guess.

255
00:09:51,884 --> 00:09:53,343
That works for cattle as well.

256
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:55,137
Oh, well, thanks for
pointing that out.

257
00:09:55,387 --> 00:09:56,387
You're welcome.

258
00:09:58,557 --> 00:10:00,434
You might want to open a window.

259
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:02,019
Oh, boy.

260
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:06,231
0h...

261
00:10:06,815 --> 00:10:09,318
J'j' whoa, oh, oh, yeah... j'j'

262
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,238
my head is so hot.

263
00:10:13,447 --> 00:10:16,075
She is such a hoot.

264
00:10:18,077 --> 00:10:19,495
- You okay?
- Fine.

265
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:22,873
Okay, don't tell me.

266
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:24,750
Missy: So hot...

267
00:10:26,043 --> 00:10:27,294
I don't like you making me out

268
00:10:27,503 --> 00:10:28,943
to be the bad guy
just 'cause I won't

269
00:10:29,004 --> 00:10:30,714
let my daughter do
whatever she wants.

270
00:10:30,923 --> 00:10:31,941
I gave you a lot of freedom,

271
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:33,258
you turned out okay.

272
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:34,760
You didn't give me freedom.

273
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:36,261
You were never around.

274
00:10:36,553 --> 00:10:37,930
Is that so?

275
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:40,641
I guarantee I made supper
for charlene and Edward

276
00:10:40,849 --> 00:10:42,009
more times than you ever did.

277
00:10:42,184 --> 00:10:43,477
I basically raised 'em.

278
00:10:43,685 --> 00:10:45,020
You think I was out dancing?

279
00:10:45,229 --> 00:10:47,029
I was out working two jobs
so your daddy could

280
00:10:47,147 --> 00:10:49,358
lose all our money on that
damn chain of fotomats!

281
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:51,628
It wasn't daddy's fault that
those little things blew over

282
00:10:51,652 --> 00:10:53,237
every time there was a storm.

283
00:10:53,445 --> 00:10:54,445
Hmm.

284
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:57,324
Seriously, I'm melting.

285
00:11:00,369 --> 00:11:01,036
George Jr.: Dead armadillo.

286
00:11:01,245 --> 00:11:02,454
That's three for me.

287
00:11:03,372 --> 00:11:05,457
This is a terrible driving game.

288
00:11:05,833 --> 00:11:07,376
Is it roadkill if
it's still twitchin'?

289
00:11:08,585 --> 00:11:11,463
Huh, both alive and dead,
just like schrodinger's cat.

290
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,298
I didn't know he had a cat.

291
00:11:13,841 --> 00:11:14,961
You've heard of schrodinger?

292
00:11:15,259 --> 00:11:16,802
Sure. It's the kid
from Charlie brown

293
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,178
who plays the piano.

294
00:11:18,387 --> 00:11:19,930
Lucy's got a crush on him.

295
00:11:20,889 --> 00:11:23,600
Schrodinger's cat
is a thought experiment.

296
00:11:23,976 --> 00:11:26,103
A cat in a box is
exposed to poison,

297
00:11:26,311 --> 00:11:28,981
and is both alive and dead
until it is observed.

298
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:30,941
So the cat's name
is schrodinger?

299
00:11:31,233 --> 00:11:32,233
No.

300
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,527
Well, what's its name?

301
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,237
Its name doesn't matter.

302
00:11:35,445 --> 00:11:36,905
It does if the cat was dead.

303
00:11:37,114 --> 00:11:39,116
Otherwise, what are you gonna
put on his tombstone?

304
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:41,243
Not likely the cat's
getting a tombstone.

305
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:42,995
It would in a pet cemetery.

306
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:46,623
Fine, the cat's name is mittens.

307
00:11:46,832 --> 00:11:48,458
Because he has
little white feet?

308
00:11:49,084 --> 00:11:50,085
Sure.

309
00:11:50,294 --> 00:11:51,670
So, in this thought experiment,

310
00:11:52,546 --> 00:11:54,423
do you think mittens
is dead or alive?

311
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:57,301
There's no way of saying
until you open the box.

312
00:11:58,260 --> 00:11:59,469
Oh, come on.

313
00:12:00,262 --> 00:12:02,764
Optimistically, I would choose
to believe he's alive.

314
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:04,725
- Yes!
- Oh, thank goodness.

315
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,435
George Jr.: Oh, dead crow.

316
00:12:06,727 --> 00:12:08,478
There ain't no doubt
about that one.

317
00:12:15,152 --> 00:12:17,070
The toilet was sanitized
for my protection.

318
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:18,822
I love this place.

319
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:21,325
Dad, can we go to reptile world?

320
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:22,826
- No.
- They got a snake

321
00:12:23,035 --> 00:12:24,912
so big it can eat
a whole chicken.

322
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,164
Oh, well, in that case, no.

323
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:29,082
- Aw.
- Let's get some sleep.

324
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:31,269
We got to get up early if we're
gonna get to cape canaveral

325
00:12:31,293 --> 00:12:32,377
in time for liftoff.

326
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:34,296
I'm so excited,
I don't know if I can.

327
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,506
Well, buddy, you're
gonna have to try, all right?

328
00:12:36,715 --> 00:12:39,009
You two share that bed,
I'll take this one.

329
00:12:39,218 --> 00:12:40,594
-Nuh-uh.

330
00:12:41,511 --> 00:12:43,096
Come on, fellas,
I'm the biggest.

331
00:12:43,305 --> 00:12:45,015
It makes sense that
I get a bed to myself.

332
00:12:46,475 --> 00:12:47,768
-Nuh-uh.

333
00:12:51,146 --> 00:12:53,315
We'll flip for it.
Georgie, call it.

334
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:54,858
Heads.

335
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:57,486
Not your day.

336
00:12:57,778 --> 00:12:58,779
Dang it.

337
00:12:59,363 --> 00:13:01,365
- That looked like heads.
- Go brush your teeth.

338
00:13:05,327 --> 00:13:06,620
This really works?

339
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:11,583
Your hair will look
just as pretty tomorrow.

340
00:13:11,959 --> 00:13:13,377
Now, come on, let's tuck you in.

341
00:13:14,962 --> 00:13:16,964
I'm glad I don't have
orange hair.

342
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:18,423
Me, too, baby.

343
00:13:18,632 --> 00:13:20,300
I want to be more like Madonna.

344
00:13:20,884 --> 00:13:21,969
Are you trying to kill me?

345
00:13:22,177 --> 00:13:23,303
'Cause if you are, good job.

346
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,227
Why is she only like a virgin?

347
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:31,795
Mary: Good night!

348
00:13:34,982 --> 00:13:36,858
You ready to finish
our conversation?

349
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:38,107
There's nothing to finish.

350
00:13:38,277 --> 00:13:40,153
I raised myself
like a jungle child.

351
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:41,362
End of story.

352
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,615
Oh, stop being so dramatic.

353
00:13:43,824 --> 00:13:44,904
You think I didn't feel bad

354
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:47,411
not being around more
than I wanted to be?

355
00:13:47,995 --> 00:13:48,995
Did you?

356
00:13:49,955 --> 00:13:51,123
A little bit.

357
00:13:52,291 --> 00:13:54,001
I'm teasing, come on.
Of course I did.

358
00:13:54,209 --> 00:13:55,889
Why else would I have
begged you and George

359
00:13:55,919 --> 00:13:57,045
to move back to medford?

360
00:13:57,254 --> 00:13:58,814
So you could be with
your grandchildren.

361
00:13:58,964 --> 00:13:59,964
And you.

362
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:01,591
- Really?
- Yeah.

363
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,945
You're the only one of my
children still talking to me.

364
00:14:03,969 --> 00:14:05,095
No surprise there.

365
00:14:05,512 --> 00:14:06,572
Besides, you raised yourself

366
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:08,140
better than I ever could.

367
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,267
You actually believe that?

368
00:14:10,726 --> 00:14:13,979
No, but it would help
my cause if you did.

369
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:23,904
Your hair looks pretty.

370
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:25,407
Enough.

371
00:14:35,167 --> 00:14:36,167
' Dad? '

372
00:14:38,086 --> 00:14:39,086
dad?

373
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:41,714
Dad?

374
00:14:42,341 --> 00:14:43,884
Dad.

375
00:14:44,343 --> 00:14:44,968
What?

376
00:14:45,177 --> 00:14:46,636
Georgie keeps kicking me.

377
00:14:47,346 --> 00:14:48,346
Kick him back.

378
00:14:48,472 --> 00:14:50,474
I'd rather not touch him.

379
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,644
You want to sleep with me?

380
00:14:54,853 --> 00:14:56,313
Yes, thank you.

381
00:14:59,983 --> 00:15:01,109
Yeah.

382
00:15:03,612 --> 00:15:04,821
Got enough room?

383
00:15:05,781 --> 00:15:07,074
Yes.

384
00:15:11,787 --> 00:15:13,705
You throw off a lot of heat.

385
00:15:14,998 --> 00:15:15,999
Sorry.

386
00:15:17,084 --> 00:15:19,795
That's all right.
It's kind of nice.

387
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,767
Do they launch those shuttles
in the rain?

388
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:36,520
I think a light rain's okay.

389
00:15:40,357 --> 00:15:41,650
Oh, no.

390
00:15:41,858 --> 00:15:42,858
It'll pass.

391
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:45,404
Just get some sleep.

392
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:54,121
It didn't pass.

393
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:56,164
Sheldon, I'm real sorry.

394
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,966
Can I tell you a secret?

395
00:16:07,217 --> 00:16:09,428
I never understood
how lightning works.

396
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:11,930
Didn't they teach you
that in high school?

397
00:16:12,139 --> 00:16:12,931
They probably did,

398
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:16,268
but I got hit in the head
a lot playing football.

399
00:16:17,936 --> 00:16:19,104
Would you explain it to me?

400
00:16:20,147 --> 00:16:23,024
Well, when positive and negative
charges grow large enough,

401
00:16:23,233 --> 00:16:25,318
a giant spark occurs
in the cloud.

402
00:16:25,527 --> 00:16:28,989
Ah, that-that's pretty cool.
What causes the thunder?

403
00:16:29,197 --> 00:16:32,993
It's a shock wave from particles
heated to 10,000 degrees.

404
00:16:33,702 --> 00:16:34,702
Interesting.

405
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,122
- You want to know what's really interesting?
- Hmm?

406
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:39,082
Aristotle thought that
the sound of thunder

407
00:16:39,291 --> 00:16:41,376
was due to a collision
between two clouds.

408
00:16:41,585 --> 00:16:43,420
He believed the clouds were
expelling air,

409
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:45,380
in the way a log on
a fire crackles...

410
00:16:45,589 --> 00:16:48,258
Adult Sheldon: I didn't realize
until years later

411
00:16:48,467 --> 00:16:50,802
that my father was
only asking questions

412
00:16:51,011 --> 00:16:53,889
about lightning and thunder
to cheer me up.

413
00:16:54,097 --> 00:16:56,516
In fact, he would often
pretend to be dumb

414
00:16:56,725 --> 00:16:58,101
just to make me feel better.

415
00:16:58,602 --> 00:17:00,061
Looks like rain.

416
00:17:00,270 --> 00:17:01,956
Adult Sheldon:
My brother, on the other hand,

417
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:03,231
didn't have to pretend.

418
00:17:11,573 --> 00:17:13,909
Okay, on the count of three,
we run to the car.

419
00:17:14,117 --> 00:17:16,453
- Ready? One, two...
- Wait.

420
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:18,079
I want shotgun going back.

421
00:17:18,622 --> 00:17:20,957
Fine, you get shotgun.
Okay, here we go.

422
00:17:21,166 --> 00:17:23,001
- One, two...
- I still think

423
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:25,045
we should wait
till the rain slows down.

424
00:17:25,253 --> 00:17:26,613
George sr.:
No, we got to get home.

425
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:28,507
I got work tomorrow,
you guys got school.

426
00:17:28,715 --> 00:17:30,133
You do realize I'll get wet?

427
00:17:30,342 --> 00:17:31,885
It's just water, Sheldon.

428
00:17:32,135 --> 00:17:34,387
All right.
Just making sure you realize.

429
00:17:35,263 --> 00:17:36,556
All right, here we go. Ready?

430
00:17:36,765 --> 00:17:38,934
One, two, three.

431
00:17:57,327 --> 00:17:59,204
Buddy, I thought we had a plan.

432
00:17:59,538 --> 00:18:00,830
You had a plan.

433
00:18:11,091 --> 00:18:12,926
N n

434
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:20,267
adult Sheldon: I never did get
to see a launch in person,

435
00:18:20,475 --> 00:18:23,311
but that was the best trip
I ever had.

436
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:31,861
I wish I had told my father
while he was alive.

